Maintaining con history:


Conversation history in agent-orchestrator flows through three layers:                                                                                                                                   
                                                                                                                                                                                                           
  1. Ingest — CS payload → typed history                                                                                                                                                                   
  native_interface.py:115 — convert_cs_to_timestamped(cs_items) converts the incoming CS conversationHistory.items into the internal timestamped_conversation_history list, seeded into the execution      
  payload at :151.                                                                                                                                                                                         
                                                                                                                                                                                                           
  2. Storage — single source of truth                                                                                                                                                                      
  execution/execution_context.py:288-314 — payload key timestamped_conversation_history is the only mutable history object (per the comment at :288, code must go through accessors, never index the       
  payload key directly):                                                                                                                                                                                   
  - get_conversation_history_timestamped() (:292) — raw list with timestamps                                                                                                                               
  - get_conversation_history_as_plain() (:302) — {role, content} pairs via to_plain() (native_agent/utils/conversation_history_utils.py)                                                                   
  - append_to_conversation_history(entry) (:306) — auto-stamps now_ms if missing                                                                                                                           
                                                                                                                                                                                                           
  Every stage that produces a turn appends here — state_manager.py:1794, openai_agent_execution_stage.py:551/578, openai_tool_postprocessor.py:253, data_collector_stage.py:27, planner2_stage.py:340/370, 
  web_search_stage.py:46, builtin_tool_handlers.py (4 call sites), skill_execution_handler.py:614, widget_action_handler.py:227, tool_refiner_stage.py:335, kg_widget_builder_stage.py:232,                
  no_answer_fallback_stage.py:91. This is how tool results and intermediate agent turns become part of the history the planners see.                                                                       
                                                                                                                                                                                                           
  3. Consumption — cleaning before it hits a prompt                                                                                                                                                        
  llm/conversation_history_utils.py (separate file from the one in native_agent/utils/) — applied by preprocessors before building planner prompts:                                                        
  - format_conversation_history() (:146) — strips/merges assistant messages via a filter registry (citations, widgets)                                                                                     
  - trim_conversation_history_to_max_user_turns() (:126) — caps how many user turns go to Planner2 (constants.DEFAULT_MAX_USER_TURNS_FOR_PLANNER2)                                                         
  - extract_user_query_from_payload() (:38) — finds the latest real user turn, skipping click-action turns                                                                                                 
                                                                                                                                                                                                           
  Persistence across turns: state_manager.py is what caches/reloads ExecutionContext (including this payload) between turns — :1794 shows it also appends directly to history during resume.               
                                                                                                                                                                                                           
